    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "518506f9_eb25d320",
        "filename": "gm/png_codec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 351,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-03T17:22:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the png_codec should take in a flag for native mode, a flag for color type, and a flag for alphamode. \n\nI\u0027m fine with using a loop so we can run all of a set of files against a particular configuration set, but I think a triply (technically quadrupley) nested loop is a smell about how this set of GMs is too broad.\n\nWe might not need to run all pngs through this entire combination set and a developer might only care about a single one if it ends up being problematic (we can create bazel test suites to group up all permutations if we like).",
      "revId": "a68618716d6e0b9084e236ae1f3662f65a07736e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3696d568_4ccfa360",
        "filename": "gm/png_codec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 351,
      "author": {
        "id": 10009
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-05T02:12:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done",
      "parentUuid": "518506f9_eb25d320",
      "revId": "a68618716d6e0b9084e236ae1f3662f65a07736e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47223773_7f39fed8",
        "filename": "gm/png_codec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 354,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-03T17:22:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this an anonymous heap allocation? Surely that\u0027s a memory leak, right?\n\nedit: I had a read (and a re-read and a re-re-read) through the Registry code to remember how it worked. Calling the Registry constructor automatically adds a pointer to the new object to the end of a linked list, so 1) Yes this must use new to put it on the heap and 2) it\u0027s not really a leak.\n\nI don\u0027t think we are going to want this mystical incantation in all calls to DEF_GM_REGISTERER_FN\n\nCan we instead have GMRegistererFn have a parameter that is a `std::function\u003cvoid\u003e(GM)` (Can be called with a GM and doesn\u0027t return anything) which hides that complexity? This callback can be called multiple times to register multiple GMs.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 354,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 354,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "a68618716d6e0b9084e236ae1f3662f65a07736e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0029b39_aabda89c",
        "filename": "gm/png_codec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 354,
      "author": {
        "id": 10009
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-05T02:12:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried passing a `std::function` as an argument that takes a `std::unique_ptr\u003cskiagm::GM\u003e`, but I ran into various issues when trying to capture a `std::unique_ptr` from a lambda. See https://stackoverflow.com/questions/8236521/how-to-capture-a-unique-ptr-into-a-lambda-expression.\n\nInstead, in https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/734163/5..6 I defined a new function, `skiagm::Register`, that takes a `skiagm::GM*` and can be called from anywhere to dynamically register a GM.",
      "parentUuid": "47223773_7f39fed8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 354,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 354,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "a68618716d6e0b9084e236ae1f3662f65a07736e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
